# 2897. Apply Operations on Array to Maximize Sum of Squares

**LeetCode Problem:** [2897. Apply Operations on Array to Maximize Sum of Squares](https://leetcode.com/problems/apply-operations-on-array-to-maximize-sum-of-squares/)

**Difficulty:** Medium

## 💡 Approach: Bit Manipulation + Greedy

### Intuition
The goal is to maximize the sum of squares of `k` numbers formed using the given array.

The key observation is that we can redistribute the set bits among the numbers to maximize the sum of their squares.

- Count the number of set bits at each bit position across all elements.
- Construct each of the `k` numbers greedily by taking every available set bit.
- Decrease the count of each bit used.
- Add the square of the constructed number to the answer, taking modulo \(10^9+7\).

This greedy strategy concentrates as many available set bits as possible into each number, maximizing the sum of squares.

## 💻 C++ Solution

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    const int MOD = 1e9 + 7;

    int maxSum(vector<int>& nums, int k) {
        vector<int> count(32, 0);

        for (const int& num : nums) {
            for (int b = 0; b < 32; b++) {
                if (num & (1 << b)) {
                    count[b]++;
                }
            }
        }

        long long ans = 0;

        while (k--) {
            long long curr = 0;

            for (int b = 0; b < 32; b++) {
                if (count[b] > 0) {
                    count[b]--;
                    curr |= (1LL << b);
                }
            }

            ans = (ans + curr * curr) % MOD;
        }

        return ans;
    }
};
```

## ⏱️ Complexity Analysis

Let:
- \(n\) = number of elements in `nums`
- \(B\) = number of bits considered (32)

**Time Complexity:** \(O(32n + 32k) = O(n+k)\), since the bit width is constant.

**Space Complexity:** \(O(32) = O(1)\), since the bit-count array has a fixed size.

